# D-FREED-INODE-HOME-NEVER-PUBLISHED-LIVE-CORE-AFTER-CLEAN-UNMOUNT, H-F13, with
# the peer-unlink reach repaired, on the disk-locking transport.  Why it
# replaces icg, the hypothesis, build (53A7F8EBBCEC0C4B6A705D2), knob,
# settings, measures and VERDICT RULES are those of
# tests/queues/ialloc_fence_reach_ab.queue, written before the first lap of
# either queue; only the configuration (2/disk/caw/direct g2b, test15 test16,
# where pha2 and pha3 measured the exposure) and the labels differ.  The two
# queues are judged separately, each by those rules.
#
# The disk-locking queue follows the TCP one through both repairs; its labels
# are iwc1..iwf3 (iyg ran the first repair and was stopped with ixg).
#
# Bound: fw3's, 1680 s per lap (icg's laps about 470 s).
#
# RERUN WITH THE CREATE-REUSE FIX IN BOTH ARMS (labels jwc1..jwf3), for the
# reason given in tests/queues/ialloc_fence_reach_ab.queue: iwc1 and iwc2 each
# shut test15 down through
# D-CREATE-REUSE-OVER-PEER-FREED-LINKED-CORPSE-SHUTS-NODE-DOWN and measured
# nothing of H-F13.  Build ~/src/mxfs-b srcversion A97F45838280C5F3B4C352C,
# NG0_CR63_DEFER=1 in both arms, the only knob between them ag_ialloc_fence;
# the verdict rules are unchanged.  No control lap on this transport has yet
# shown the cause, so the controls keep their three laps.
# Every lap here is also an H-L1 fix lap for the create-reuse defect on this
# transport: its CRESULT line is graded by
# tests/queues/cr63_linked_defer_caw_ab.queue's rules, in either arm
# (cr63_linked_defer is 1 in both; declared before the first lap).
1680 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots NG0_CR63_DEFER=1 NG0_IALLOC_FENCE=0 NG0_PEER_UNLINK=300 NG0_DRAIN_BOUND=0 NG0_PUBCLAIM_GUARD=1 NG0_PUBCLAIM_DELAY_MS=200 NG0_CREATE_PARENT_DELAY_MS=5 NG0_SELFCLOBBER_GUARD=1 NG0_MIRROR_CHECK=1 NG0_RECYCLE_GUARD=1 NG0_FRESHSRC_GUARD=1 NG0_DELAY_MS=0 NG0_IFREE_DRAIN=1 NG0_IFREE_REAP=1 tests/noino_gen0_ab.sh jwc1 1 300 2/disk/caw/direct g2b
